~ hotel_california
# TODO: Uh oh, no ngettext() support in Dialogue Manager...
match GameState.quest.inventory.items.size():
	when 1:
		{{player_name}}: I’d better take this thread to the Eternal Loom first.
	else:
		{{player_name}}: I’d better take these threads to the Eternal Loom first.
=> END

~ arun
if not GameState.quest:
	# Player is not on a quest ⇒ they finished the tutorial!
	% Wend WovenWay: It's so good to be in Fray's End again!
	% Wend WovenWay: Thank you for traveling here with me.
# TODO: Use an object at the root of the scene rather than hardcoding this path?
else:
	if GameState.quest.quest_path == "res://scenes/quests/lore_quests/quest_000/quest.tres":
		Wend WovenWay: We made it, StoryWeaver! Fray's End is just across the bridge.
	Wend WovenWay: Take the threads you've collected to the Eternal Loom.
=> END

~ marie
if void_quest_unlocker.is_satisfied():
	Rue RuffleRhyme: You must have been to visit Moss!
	Rue RuffleRhyme: We saw the Void retreating from the West End path!
else:
	Rue RuffleRhyme: Oh, are you trying to get to the West End?
	Rue RuffleRhyme: That path has been blocked by the Void for years.
	Rue RuffleRhyme: Our cat is really upset about it. She used to love going over there.
	Rue RuffleRhyme: Please find Moss the Monk. She might be able to help you push back the Void!
=> END

~ farmer
Pru PloughPleat: Seeds have terrible dating lives...
Pru PloughPleat: They always get stood up!
Pru PloughPleat: Hahahahahaha!
{{player_name}}: ...
Pru PloughPleat: Guess it was only funny in my head.
